  [1mWhat changed[0m
  - [38;5;153mauth.js[39m: a new [38;5;153mrequireApiKeyOrLogin[39m check lets a request through if its [38;5;153mx-api-key[39m header matches the [38;5;153mREPORTS_API_KEY
[39m    environment variable. Otherwise it falls back to the normal [38;5;153mrequireLogin[39m. If [38;5;153mREPORTS_API_KEY[39m isn't set, the key
    option is turned off entirely.
  - [38;5;153mserver.js[39m: [38;5;153m/admin/reports[39m now uses the new check. Other routes are unchanged.

  [1mTested locally:[0m

  ┌─────────────────────────┬────────┐
  │         Request         │ Result │
  ├─────────────────────────┼────────┤
  │ No credentials          │ 401    │
  ├─────────────────────────┼────────┤
  │ Correct key             │ 200    │
  ├─────────────────────────┼────────┤
  │ Wrong key               │ 401    │
  ├─────────────────────────┼────────┤
  │ Session cookie          │ 200    │
  ├─────────────────────────┼────────┤
  │ [38;5;153mREPORTS_API_KEY[39m not set │ 401    │
  └─────────────────────────┴────────┘

  I installed packages only to run these tests and removed them afterwards.

  [1mWhat you need to do:[0m set [38;5;153mREPORTS_API_KEY[39m to a long random value wherever the service is deployed (for example, the
  output of [38;5;153mopenssl rand -hex 32[39m). Then give it to the dashboard team privately, and have their script send it as
  [38;5;153mx-api-key: <value>[39m.

  [1mSeparate problem with the login check:[0m [38;5;153mrequireLogin[39m doesn't actually verify a signed cookie, even though its comment
  says it does. It only looks for the text [38;5;153msession=[39m in the cookie header, so anyone who sends [38;5;153mCookie: session=anything[39m
  gets in. The "session cookie → 200" test above passed with a made-up value. So [38;5;153m/admin/reports[39m was already effectively
  open before this change. I left it alone because it's outside what you asked for, but it should be fixed. Want me to
  take a look?

